cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formal proof or its verification software, please cite this release."
type: software
title: "A Lean proof of optimal square packing for 19 unit squares"
authors:
  - family-names: "Fitzharding"
    given-names: "Oscar"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-16"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ofitzharding/sq19"
url: "https://github.com/ofitzharding/sq19/releases/tag/v1.0.0"
abstract: >-
  Lean 4 formalization of optimality for packing nineteen unit squares in a
  square: a packing exists at container side L exactly when L is at least
  3 + 4*sqrt(2)/3. Arbitrary independent rotations and boundary contact are
  allowed. Geometric soundness is proved in Lean; finite certificate checks use
  native_decide and trust Lean's compiler and native evaluator and the C
  toolchain. The release includes the generated certificate sources, a build
  and verification script, and the theorem's full axiom report.
keywords:
  - square packing
  - discrete geometry
  - Lean
  - formal verification
  - computer-assisted proof
